# Coding Style

## Immutability (Critical)

Always create new objects, never mutate existing ones.

Rationale: Immutable data prevents hidden side effects, makes debugging easier, and is essential for React state correctness.

## File Organization

Many small files over few large files:
- 200–400 lines typical, 800 max
- High cohesion, low coupling
- Extract utilities when a file grows
- Organize by feature/domain, not by type

## Error Handling

Handle errors explicitly at every level:
- Never silently swallow errors
- Provide user-facing messages in UI code
- Log detailed context on the server side
- Fail fast with clear messages

## Input Validation

Always validate at system boundaries:
- All user input before processing
- All external data (API responses, file uploads, GPX content)
- Use schema-based validation where available
- Never trust external data

## Code Quality Checklist

Before marking any task complete:
- [ ] Functions are small (under 50 lines)
- [ ] Files are focused (under 800 lines)
- [ ] No deep nesting (over 4 levels)
- [ ] Errors are handled explicitly
- [ ] No hardcoded magic values
- [ ] No mutation of existing objects
- [ ] No `console.log` left in production code
